00:10:13.182 --> 00:10:14.931
Persistence and durability:

229
00:10:15.211 --> 00:10:23.595
Redis is in-memory, with optional RDB snapshots and an AOF log (appendfsync everysec can lose ~1 s of writes).

230
00:10:23.875 --> 00:10:32.942
Treat it as a cache or ephemeral store unless you've deliberately configured and tested durability, and even then prefer it for data you can rebuild.

231
00:10:33.222 --> 00:10:34.033
Scaling:

232
00:10:34.313 --> 00:10:39.113
Redis Cluster shards keys across 16,384 hash slots.

233
00:10:39.393 --> 00:10:43.681
Multi-key operations need the keys in the same slot (use hash tags:

234
00:10:43.961 --> 00:10:47.246
BLR:riders:geo, BLR:riders:lastseen).

235
00:10:48.596 --> 00:10:51.519
Document stores: embedding versus referencing.

236
00:10:51.799 --> 00:10:53.441
