589
00:27:53.338 --> 00:27:56.197
Sequence: happy path, one ping to all stores.

590
00:27:56.477 --> 00:27:59.271
The sequence diagram walks through it step by step.

591
00:27:59.551 --> 00:28:00.490
R to TI:

592
00:28:00.770 --> 00:28:03.735
POST or pings lat,lng,ts,seq (batched).

593
00:28:04.015 --> 00:28:07.877
TI to TI: validate (bounds, speed sanity), server timestamp.

594
00:28:08.157 --> 00:28:12.039
TI to K: produce key=riderId (acks=all).

595
00:28:12.319 --> 00:28:13.301
TI to R:

596
00:28:13.581 --> 00:28:14.669
202.

597
00:28:14.949 --> 00:28:17.829
K to LW: batch of 500 pings.

598
00:28:18.109 --> 00:28:21.074
LW to RD: one Lua call per batch:

599
00:28:21.354 --> 00:28:24.234
HSET if newer seq, GEOADD, ZADD lastseen.

600
00:28:24.514 --> 00:28:26.733
LW to K: commit offsets.

601
00:28:27.013 --> 00:28:29.935
K to HW: batch of 500 pings.

602
00:28:30.215 --> 00:28:36.850
HW to CS: async INSERTs (idempotent: same PK = same row), LOCALQUORUM.

603
00:28:37.130 --> 00:28:40.309
HW to K: commit offsets after all acks.

604
00:28:44.159 --> 00:28:47.999
Sequence: failure path, Cassandra degraded, Redis unaffected.

605
00:28:48.279 --> 00:28:51.073
The sequence diagram walks through it step by step.

606
00:28:51.353 --> 00:28:53.081
K to LW: pings.

607
00:28:53.361 --> 00:28:57.820
LW to RD: writes OK (dispatch + tracking unaffected).

608
00:28:58.100 --> 00:28:59.913
K to HW: pings.

609
00:29:00.193 --> 00:29:01.644
HW to CS:

610
00:29:01.924 --> 00:29:05.807
INSERT LOCALQUORUM, then 2 of 3 replicas ack, then OK.

611
00:29:06.087 --> 00:29:07.537
HW to CS:

612
00:29:07.817 --> 00:29:09.460
INSERT, then WriteTimeout.

613
00:29:09.740 --> 00:29:15.009
HW to HW: retry with backoff (idempotent), do NOT commit offsets.

614
00:29:15.289 --> 00:29:17.465
CS to HW: recovers.

615
00:29:17.745 --> 00:29:21.457
HW to CS: catch up from Kafka at max throughput.

616
00:29:21.737 --> 00:29:26.751
HW to HW: accept gap, alert, history missing for that window.

617
00:29:30.601 --> 00:29:31.347
Note:

618
00:29:31.627 --> 00:29:34.401
What the system guarantees after this failure path.

619
00:29:34.681 --> 00:29:41.827
A degraded history store never affects latest-position or dispatch, because each sink has its own consumer group.

620
00:29:42.107 --> 00:29:57.339
History is eventually complete as long as the outage is shorter than Kafka retention (3 days), since the writer only commits offsets after writes are acknowledged, and duplicate writes on retry are harmless (same primary key, then same row).

621
00:29:57.619 --> 00:30:02.547
Delivery evidence for disputes lives in PostgreSQL, not in the history store.

622
00:30:03.897 --> 00:30:06.543
State: a rider's presence in the geo index.

623
