664
00:32:15.987 --> 00:32:18.291
Item, and Calculation, and Result.

665
00:32:18.571 --> 00:32:19.573
Peak pings.

666
00:32:19.853 --> 00:32:20.920
Calculation:

667
00:32:21.200 --> 00:32:23.739
80 K riders ÷ 4 s.

668
00:32:24.019 --> 00:32:24.829
Result:

669
00:32:25.109 --> 00:32:28.437
20 K per second (normal peak 10 K per second).

670
00:32:28.717 --> 00:32:29.784
Kafka ingress.

671
00:32:30.064 --> 00:32:31.131
Calculation:

672
00:32:31.411 --> 00:32:34.696
20 K per second times ~150 B.

673
00:32:34.976 --> 00:32:40.949
Result: ~3 MB per second; 48 partitions give consumer parallelism headroom.

674
00:32:41.229 --> 00:32:42.275
Redis memory.

675
00:32:42.555 --> 00:32:43.621
Calculation:

676
00:32:43.901 --> 00:32:51.411
80 K riders times (~150 B hash + ~60 B geo + ~40 B lastseen).

677
00:32:51.691 --> 00:32:54.080
Result: ~20 MB: trivial.

678
00:32:54.360 --> 00:32:55.363
Redis ops.

679
00:32:55.643 --> 00:32:56.709
Calculation:

680
00:32:56.989 --> 00:33:00.360
20 K pings per second times 3 ops (pipelined).

681
00:33:00.640 --> 00:33:07.893
Result: ~60 K ops per second: a single shard can do it, cluster of 3 shards for headroom and HA.

682
00:33:08.173 --> 00:33:09.368
Cassandra writes.

683
00:33:09.648 --> 00:33:10.715
Calculation:

684
00:33:10.995 --> 00:33:13.363
20 K per second times 2 tables.

685
00:33:13.643 --> 00:33:14.453
Result:

686
00:33:14.733 --> 00:33:16.781
40 K rows per second at peak.

687
00:33:18.131 --> 00:33:19.433
Cassandra storage.

688
00:33:19.713 --> 00:33:31.297
Calculation: ~10 K per second avg times 86,400 times 2 tables times ~100 B times RF 3 times 7 days.

689
00:33:31.577 --> 00:33:37.209
Result: ~3.6 TB raw, then ~1.2 TB with compression.

690
00:33:37.489 --> 00:33:38.683
Cassandra nodes.

691
00:33:38.963 --> 00:33:45.129
Calculation: ~15 to 20 K writes per second per node comfortably (to be load-tested).

692
00:33:45.409 --> 00:33:46.219
Result:

693
00:33:46.499 --> 00:33:48.782
6 nodes (RF 3) with headroom.

694
00:33:49.062 --> 00:33:50.299
Partition size.

695
00:33:50.579 --> 00:33:51.646
Calculation:

696
00:33:51.926 --> 00:33:55.595
10,800 pings or shift times 100 B.

697
00:33:55.875 --> 00:33:58.414
Result: ~1 MB per (rider, day).

